// Title: QTFY Proxy Platform Management binaries and staged Clash on Linux endpoints
// Id: 2cea0f94-f742-4e1e-9db7-5e57bd76a759
// MITRE: T1090.003 (Multi-hop Proxy), T1036.005 (Match Legitimate Name or Location), T1105 (Ingress Tool Transfer)
// Reference: https://www.ic3.gov/CSA/2026/260826.pdf
// Author: Jarmi
// Date: 2026-08-27
// Tested on: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting (DeviceProcessEvents, DeviceFileEvents) with Defender for Endpoint on Linux
// FP notes: Routers and IoT devices that run custom OpenWrt will not appear in Defender telemetry; hunt those through network logs and firmware inventory instead. Developer workstations may legitimately run Clash.
let lookback = 90d;
let qtfy_hashes = dynamic([
    "0cf8ed7064d3d4827f841451c661d788d4cf7d067901e35a7a019f1c9d5ef656",
    "c46944343b7e33c0f88ca9583b8145a4735d6e9780f9df1777b4c59887b56a35",
